## Ability groups
Design differentiated activities for three groups based on current mastery:
- **Foundation** (below 40%) — needs scaffolding, concrete examples, guided practice
- **Core** (40–70%) — consolidating understanding, needs application with some challenge
- **Extension** (above 70%) — ready to deepen, connect, or apply knowledge in novel contexts

## Time budget
Total lesson: **{{ duration_minutes }} minutes**
- Starter: ~{{ (duration_minutes * 0.10) | round | int }} min
- Introduction & key concepts: ~{{ (duration_minutes * 0.15) | round | int }} min
- Main differentiated activity: ~{{ (duration_minutes * 0.50) | round | int }} min
- Formative check: ~{{ (duration_minutes * 0.10) | round | int }} min
- Plenary: ~{{ (duration_minutes * 0.15) | round | int }} min

## Your task
Generate a complete, practical lesson plan a teacher can pick up and use immediately. Be specific — name actual activities, not vague suggestions. Connect activities to student interests wherever possible. Include at least two real-world applications of the subtopic(s).

